    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "While drive-through diners are a classic icon of 1950's America, the actual concept of the \"drive-through\" has seen little to no improvement since then, making it an outdated relic in comparison to today's cars and today's technologically-advanced world. To envision the drive-through of the future is to bring unheralded advances in efficiency, accuracy, and usability--so many, in fact, that your current drive-through experience will forever pale in comparison to what you see can be possible.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
